  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $-10x+5y\\ge -5?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x+5y & \\ge -5 \\\\ 5y & \\ge 10x-5 \\\\ y & \\ge 2x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=2x-1.$ Since the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=2x-1$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a solid line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y\\ge 2x-1$ refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line $y=2x-1,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/a9eef4f75cb108bd00fa1230a4be9f5b9edfc21d0ff7f999a3ca8aeb212f08b7.png)",
